ce by Protected Status (Under Exceptional Drought)\nIn 2024, under severe drought conditions, sites located **within or adjacent to protected or high-biodiversity-value areas** accounted for the majority of total reforested area (14.81 ha of 19.78 ha) due to Buenavista del Cobre, but recorded the lowest net gain ratios (ranging from **0 to 0.08**) because of larger impacted areas and zero reforestation at La Caridad and Charcas. Conversely, the only site to achieve a net gain $>1.0$ in 2024 (**Nueva Rosita**, at **3.4**) was located outside protected areas [IDS24_ESP_06_Ambiental_ebook p.106].\n\n| Site | Protected / High-Biodiversity Status | 2024 Reforested Area (ha) | 2024 Plants Reforested | 2024 Impacted Area (ha) | 2024 Net Gain Value (Restored / Impacted) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Within or Adjacent to Protected / High-Biodiversity Areas** | | **14.81 ha** | **12,778** | **344.36 ha** | **0.03 \u2013 0.08** |\n| **M\u00e9xico: Buenavista del Cobre** | **Within:** Ramsar Site No. 2044 (Ecosistema Ajos-Bavispe), RTP-41 Cananea-San Pedro, AICA No. 126, KBA Sistema de Sierras de la Sierra Madre Occidental | 13.22 | 12,578 | 159.46 | 0.08 |\n| **M\u00e9xico: La Caridad** | **Within:** RTP-44 Bavispe-El Tigre, AICA No. 126, KBA Sistema de Sierras de la Sierra Madre Occidental<br>**Adjacent:** ANP \u00c1rea de protecci\u00f3n de flora y fauna Bavispe | \u2014 | \u2014 | 121.98 | \u2014 |\n| **M\u00e9xico: Charcas** | **Within:** KBA Sierra Catorce | \u2014 | \u2014 | 2.60 | \u2014 |\n| **Per\u00fa: Cuajone** | KBA Cerro Los Calatos-Torata | 1.59 | 200 | 60.32 | 0.03 |\n| **Outside Protected / High-Biodiversity Areas** | | **4.97 ha** | **4,071** | **36.09 ha** | **0.03 \u2013 3.40** |\n| **M\u00e9xico: Nueva Rosita** | Not within or adjacent to protected / high-biodiversity areas | 3.40 | 2,408 | \u2014 | 3.4 |\n| **M\u00e9xico: San Mart\u00edn** | Not within or adjacent to protected / high-biodiversity areas | 0.45 | 490 | 3.60 | 0.13 |\n| **Per\u00fa: Toquepala** | Not within or adjacent to protected / high-biodiversity areas | 1.12 | 1,173 | 32.49 | 0.03 |\n\n*(Source: [IDS24_ESP_06_Ambiental_ebook p.106])*", "expectedOutput": "If droughts worsen in 2025, the sites plan to implement new strategies such as technified irrigation systems to mitigate drought impacts. As of 2024, reforestation and net gain rates vary by site and their proximity to protected or high-biodiversity areas. For example, Buenavista del Cobre (inside several protected areas) reforested 13.22 ha (net gain 0.08), whereas Nueva Rosita (not adjacent to protected areas) reforested 3.40 ha (net gain 3.4). Generally, sites within or near protected areas have lower net gain ratios due to higher impacted areas, while sites outside these zones may achieve higher net gains. If droughts intensify, success will depend on the effectiveness of new irrigation strategies, but areas in or near protected habitats might remain more challenging for net habitat gain due to stricter conservation standards and potentially greater drought vulnerability.", "context": ["troducci\u00f3r\n\nH\u00e1bitats restaurados 0 proteaidos\n\nCii 2024+ Tu scquiu GxCCNCiuFIuI Uiculu TTuEoiu cupuciuuu puru CuifpM TuiNecu\nde deforestaci\u00f3n neta cero; sin embargo; para 2025 implementaremos nuevas estrategias para mitigar Ia sequ\u00eda como el uso de sistemas de riego tecnificado\n\n| Unidad | M\u00e9xico: Buenavista del Cobre | M\u00e9xico: La Caridad | M\u00e9xico: Nueva Rosita | M\u00e9xico: San Mart\u00edn | M\u00e9xico: Charcas | Per\u00fa: Toquepala | Per\u00fa: Cuajone |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Nombre del \u00e1rea protegida o de alto valor de biodiversidad | **Dentro:**<br>\u2022 Sitio Ramsar No. 2044 Ecosistema Ajos-Bavispe, zona de influencia Cuenca R\u00edo San Pedro<br>\u2022 RTP-41 Cananea-San Pedro<br>\u2022 AICA No. 126, Sistema de Sierras de la Sierra Madre Occidental<br>\u2022 KBA Sistema de Sierras de la Sierra Madre Occidental | **Dentro:**<br>\u2022 